 \section*{Data and Code Availability}
 
-3DMSL \cite{ref12} and MitoEM \cite{ref15} are publicly available. The accompanying reproducibility package supplies mesh/occupancy per-object tables, reconstructed development coefficients and scaling, split IDs, calibration bounds, boundary replay results, phase/tie/topology diagnostics, input and output hashes, analysis scripts, revised notebooks, and the archived and corrected Section 24 validation outputs. The added package records all 360 intervention condition rows, the 330 non-pilot rows, failed boundary fits, input hashes, and corrected model-sensitivity results. Deterministic reconstruction with the recorded seed reproduces the reported correction metrics and coverage counts. The package now includes the original frozen run, its model, split IDs, stored predictions, and protocol. The supplied model's full SHA-256 matches the recorded hash (prefix 93b6daed), and all five protocol-listed input hashes match. Applying that model to the archived descriptors, without refitting, reproduced all 2,728 stored occupancy-only residuals to within $7\times10^{-14}$ percentage points. Original artifacts and locally reconstructed models are stored separately. This verifies artifact consistency, not the chronology of every analytical decision. A result-to-file map identifies supporting code and outputs. The package additionally preserves the executed Section 25 notebook and its saved summaries. Its containment results were checked against those summaries; the new containment-specific per-object records were not supplied for independent reaggregation. The package distinguishes original reported results, local reproductions, and post-audit exploratory diagnostics. Reproduction covers the primary correction and selected boundary and resolution diagnostics; it is not an end-to-end rerun of every notebook analysis. No public repository DOI is claimed.
